    "knowledge_point": "Evaluating the Definite Integral of a Rational Function",
    "problem": "${\\int }_{-3}^{-1}{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
    "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{-4+1}}{(-4+1)}{|}_{-3}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-3}}{(-3)}{|}_{-3}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}{|}_{-3}^{-1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{3(-1)^{3}}-\\frac{1}{3(-3)^{3}}) \\\\  & =-(-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{81}) \\\\  & =-(-\\frac{26}{81}) \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{81}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
